+# Ticket546 compatible JSON decode cost
+
+Bounded delegated change from00144921; implementation67f65945. Root owns wiring retained observer/cache/monitor callsites after integration. The new `decode_json` seam uses msgspec only for decoding; on DecodeError or UnicodeError it delegates to stdlib json.loads, retaining legacy NaN/Infinity, lone surrogate and overflowingfloat behavior plus malformedinput exception types. Encoders and canonical digests remain unchanged; strict finite persistence still rejects nonfinite values. Dependency msgspec>=0.22,<0.23 is measured, not speculative.
+
+Private binary-wheel-only msgspec0.22.0 benchmark ran as codex-daemon-test UID1017 under CPython3.12.3. Actual synthetic361KB formatting state and469KB snapshot, five repeats of100 decodes per arm, CPU process_time timer, ABBA stdlib/msgspec/msgspec/stdlib. Original inputs were explicitly `open(...).read()` strings, matching retained resource/formatstate inputs. Format STR stdlib .199893/.243107s vs msgspec .081509/.078863s; snapshot STR stdlib .334471/.342507s vs msgspec .111592/.129735s. About2.45-3.08x faster. Supplemental BYTES runs: format stdlib .227263/.192643s vs msgspec .095653/.103415s; snapshot stdlib .385823/.276575s vs msgspec .214099/.112203s. Bytes runs varied more, but confirmed improvement. Both paths assert semantic equality against the actual existing artifacts. Raw private payloads were never emitted. Receipts `/tmp/wake547-results/msgspec546-benchmark.json` and `/tmp/wake547-results/msgspec546-str-bytes-benchmark.json` retained separately.
+
+Primary docs [supported types](https://msgspec.dev/supported-types) document arbitrary-size JSON integers. The same page states msgspec JSON encoding converts nonfinite floats to null; this is why this change uses no msgspec encoder. Binary wheels installed for CPython3.11/3.12 using --only-binary=:all:, noRust/Cargo/sourcebuild. Qualification package resolver must include the new dependency; --no-deps cannot establish a complete installation.
+
+Public decoder seam `PYTHONPATH=src:tests /tmp/wake216-py311/bin/python -m unittest test_json_decode`: initialred missing new module; green4 cases. Golden literal expectations protect integer2^100+1, negativezero, criticalfloatroundtrips, Unicode/escapedUnicode/tmuxliterals, UTF8bytes, legacyNaN/±Inf/1e999/surrogatefallback, independently owned nestedcontainers and stdlib JSONDecodeError/UnicodeDecodeError. The old decoder had no known value correctness defect; performance motivation is independently measured above. Codec4PASS bothPython.
