+# Ticket546 native redraw cost
+
+Bounded performance repair from127b4dc7; implementation6a0c2e6e. Parent steady profile identified29nativecommands in10ticks, including9 separate `refresh-client -S` children outside20finite option batches. The background formatter now relies on stock tmux option-write redraw when its transport is a qualified TmuxTransport (including retained snapshot wrapper). Explicit CLI and non-tmux/Psmux adapters retain their existing refresh call. No persistent command client was introduced.
+
+Primary source proof, stock tmux3.4: [cmd-set-option.c](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tmux/tmux/3.4/cmd-set-option.c) line212 calls options_push_changes after a successful option change; [options.c](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tmux/tmux/3.4/options.c) lines1103-1108 update session status caches and schedule redraw for attached clients. These native effects already cover background formatting writes.
+
+Public seam command: `PYTHONPATH=src:tests /tmp/wake216-py311/bin/python -m unittest test_tab_format_process_budget.FormattingProcessBudgetTests.test_two_dirty_windows_share_native_batches_and_keep_current_lease`. Red5nativeprocesses exceeded limit4 before the fix. Green4 afterfix, .207s. The same test now attaches an owned real tmux terminal through a160-column PTY, observes actual RUN bytes arrive without any refresh-client command, verifies native lease unchanged, selective PID fencing, bounded session/window batches and rollback. PTY client and private server are cleaned up. This is native attached-terminal proof, not merely a display-message projection.
+
+Focused local selection `PYTHONPATH=src:tests /tmp/wake216-py311/bin/python -m unittest discover -s tests -p 'test_tab_format*.py'`:72PASS17.648s. Same command with `/tmp/wake216-py312/bin/python`:72PASS17.006s. Logs `/tmp/native-redraw546-py311.log` and `/tmp/native-redraw546-py312.log`. `git diff --check` passed. HostedCI skipped under costpolicy. No broadreview, post-reviewremediation or production effects; full ownerCPU qualification remains with primaryowner.
