+# Ticket546 retained readonly formatting channel
+
+Source base36f42dbe. Implementation8ca02134; environment-preserving attachment followupddc2a95b. This is a separate source qualification for a new formatting read adapter, not borrowed metadata-feed proof. Full immutable installed source/wheel and60+60 CPU qualification remain with ticket547. No broad review, post-review remediation or production effect.
+
+One deep module exposes read(commands,deadline), close and status. The retained TabObserver owner lazily creates one read-only/no-output/ignore-size stock tmux controlclient per eligible workspace only when managed formatting options are read. `-E` prevents session environment imports. Generic CLI, Psmux, pane capture and all writer paths remain unchanged. Status records workspace/state/ownedPID/request/failurecounts separately under observer.formatting_reads; it provides no activity evidence. Ownership hooks are removed and only owned children reaped on owner configuration replacement and stop.
+
+The module validates user-owned socket inode/UID on every request, permits only fixed managed show-options and exactwindow display-message reads, limits128 commands/7arguments/128characters perargument and1MiB output, clamps requests to2s, and uses nonblocking stdin writes guarded by the same absolute deadline. Every fixed read has an unpredictable marker command. Data is recovered from the real begin header through the LAST matching end before its marker frame; hostile protocol-looking option payload is retained. Matching marker begin/end identities are verified. UTF8 plus universal newline decoding matches existing subprocess text=True behavior. Read errors are unknown and invalidate the channel with bounded reconnect backoff; no mutation is sent or replayed through this adapter.
+
+Native source tests cover hostile fake begin/end payload pairs, CR/CRLF/LF, quotes/Unicode/dollar/backslash, full option-value equality to existing native adapter, clientflags and unchanged panePIDs/focus/layout; warmed reads avoid subprocesses while writes/capture retain them. Whitelist and oversizedidentity rejection create no client. Socket replacement closes only the owned reader and preserves the replacement server. Expired deadlines create no child. Actual128×8192B read output exceeds1MiB and closes the reader. A deliberately stopped PRIVATE fixture server exercises a128command request with50ms deadline; it returns timeout and reaps the owned client within.8s. Control stdio is served by the tmux server, so stopping clientPID alone does not stall the protocol.
+
+A real TabMonitor fixture proves disabled formatting leaves reader idle with noPID, enable creates the readclient, config replacement reaps the oldPID and opens a distinct reader, and stop reaps both channels while leaving fixture panes alive. Native environment case sets a session update-environment fixture variable to session-value and child env to monitor-value: before-E it fails with monitor-value; after-E bothPython retain session-value.
