+Equal-work CPU benchmark uses the CURRENT _command_batch adapter (ONE subprocess percohort) versus the warmed retained reader. Both process identical40fixedreadonly commands (session+2windows), assert identical outputs for every request, ABBA100requests perarm. Includes RUSAGE_SELF, reaped childCPU and /proc liveownedclient CPU. Subprocess totals .480163/.518310CPU s vs retained .083822/.096030s; estimated saved .00396-.00422CPU/request, not a whole-owner acceptance result. Exact metrics retained in ticket546-read-channel-cost.json. Live controlclient CPU was0.00s at kernel tick resolution; server work is outside this owned-client microbenchmark in both arms. The earlier /tmp/read-channel-benchmark546.json omitted live-client accounting and is retained only as preliminary evidence. Script locator /tmp/read-channel-ownedcpu-benchmark546.py; native tmux3.4/CPython3.11.15.
